# Tell Josh about every gap you record

This is a **must-do** rule (Josh, November 1).

Whenever you write a gap, limitation, known failure, missing behaviour, risk or
open decision into a document, commit message, ledger entry or test README, say
it to Josh in plain words in the same turn. Say what breaks for him, not just
where it's written down.

On November 1 the codec work recorded three media gaps (WebAudio AAC,
Widevine host signatures, implicitly signalled HE-AAC) in the docs. Only one of
them was mentioned in chat, in passing. Josh found the others himself on GitHub.
A gap that lives only in the docs looks like it was hidden.

- Put new gaps in your reply, near the top, not buried after a success summary.
- If an agent reports gaps, pass them on to Josh when you relay its result.
  "Not run or tested yet" is status, not a gap: say it once in a short line,
  not in the gap list. Don't pad the list with speculative security notes.
- Gaps are part of the work he asked for. Say whether you're fixing it now,
  and if not, why not and what it would take.
